A||N||25||fropuff||I'm a little nervous...||||1||
Z||000000||fropuff||02-11-2001||10:48 AM||||Hey, yesterday I turned 16, and tomorrow I'm going for my driver's test.  I'm pretty nervous.  I want to get it the first attempt, just like anyone else.  I was wondering if anyone has any hints for me or things for me to look for; things they fail you for.  I have to get used to stopping before the sign; I know that, just can't do it.  Thanks a lot for any help.  <P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000001||KRMFiero||02-11-2001||11:05 AM||||pray that you will pass before you go to bed<P>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000002||blayde8||02-11-2001||11:30 AM||||Don't worry, you'll be fine.  I took my test back in October and it was one of the easiest things I've ever done.  I passed on my first try and barely got any points knocked off.  I think I only got 2 knocked off when taking a turn onto a one-way street I went to the far side.  They are really picky though, they'll try to get you for anything.  Let us know how you did.||||reg||14
Z||000003||Old Lar||02-11-2001||11:44 AM||||Don't speed!!!!  <BR>If you know the route watch out for school zone speed limits.<BR>Use turn signals!<BR>Make sure you stop behind the stop sign, not in the crosswalk.<BR>Do you have to do a K turn, parallel park?<BR>Brake gently, no panic stops.<BR>Stay in your lane.<BR>Two hands on the wheel.||||reg||10
Z||000004||FieroLisa||02-11-2001||11:55 AM||||I was so nervous that I almost failed, but for a pretty dumb reason: braking too early, braking too long, and going to slow. My mom had a geo metro rented since our van was broken down, so I drove that in the test. I started turning the wrong way in the cones manueverability, but since the car was so small I righted myself and got throught that with a perfect score. Oh well at least I passed..it still took me forever to learn to drive the Fiero!<P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>Tarheels Fieros Website</A><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/pffsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||JohnnyK||02-11-2001||12:30 PM||||They'll get you for small things that you wouldn;t think of. I know lots of people who have failed because they didn't look left and right at railway crossings and things like that, and if you get stuck turning left and it turns red, your doomed.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||fropuff||02-11-2001||12:38 PM||||The parking that they require is a 90 degree backing and parallel.  I was good at them when I took behind-the-wheel a few months ago, and now I kind of forgot what to do.  I'll figure it out.  This drivers exam place is new; I've heard that they pass almost anyone, but still...  They will fail you for not stopping before the sidewalk when coming out of the parking lot.  Gotta watch out for that.  I get nervous around stop lights when I have to turn, whether it's green or not.  They knock off points for not signaling 100 feet prior, etc.  Gotta watch out for those signs, though.  Thanks for the help.  Keep 'em comin'!<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000007||sqoach||02-11-2001||01:03 PM||||been 3 years, but i still remember everything. first they checked my car out (not my fiero, didn't own one then)<BR>made sure all turn signals worked, and brake lights. be sure to buckle up first, check your mirrors, and turn off the radio for sure.<BR>everything else has already been said. except if you have to park, parallel park, whatever, make sure to use your parking brake. they got me for that. i didn't know i had to do that with an auto.<P>good luck.<P>almost forgot, don't be nervous. they can sense that and then they will make you do something to where you have to think a lot and try to screw you up. (that's what the guy here did) just relax, keep your hands at 10-2 and you'll do fine.<BR>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mysig2.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by sqoach (edited 02-11-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000008||My7Fieros||02-11-2001||01:16 PM||||I took my d/l test in Jan of 88.....cant quite remember, but I do recall it being pretty easy. Good luck!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://tgowens.com/My7Fieros_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Black88GT||02-11-2001||02:52 PM||||I have a 2 funny driving test stories.  Before I took my test, I was watching this other kid take his.  He had this big ole Chevy Conversion van, and I was thinking how the hell is he going to parallel park that boat? The parking part is the last thing you do. He nailed it perfectly.  The only problem was, after you pull out of the parking box there is a stop sign, and he was too excited to stop I guess because he ran right through it.  Automatic failure....<P>When I took mine, I had this really old instructor.  The first thing on the course is to back up straight, then a 3 point turn, then parking.  There are stop signs and cones and such you have to watch out for.  So anyway, I backed up straight, and the instructor told me to do the 3 point turn.  So I did it, then I pulled out, stopped at the sign, and went to parallel park.  I parallel parked, but the instructor wasn't saying anything.  I look over, he is asleep!<BR>I just pulled into the spot a little then pulled out, stopped and the sign, then woke him up.  I was like OK I'm done, and he was like uh yeah ok pull over there so I can give you your paperwork.  Never even used parallel parking at all.<P>I'm looking forward to the motorcycle test coming up...<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||7
Z||000010||btoth||02-11-2001||04:02 PM||||The first thing the guy did after getting in the car with me was turn the radio on and recline his seat all the way back... maybe he was nervous too?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I was really nervouse adbout speeding... I can't seem to drive slower than 35 but I got stuck behind someone doing 20. Passed easy... three rights and a left on some curvy back roads and then the manueverabilty test which was so much easier without some dumb instructor yelling at you for hitting the cones.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000011||hugh||02-11-2001||06:00 PM||||I passed my test easily many,many years ago,but do you know how hard it is to parallel park a horse.Seriously,if you weren't nervous when you were practicing you shouldn't be nervous when taking your test.The testers know through experience you are nervous and if they are good also know if you should pass.You won't be nervous after the test,so don't be nervous before it!Best of luck.||||reg||1
Z||000012||rogergarrison||02-11-2001||06:31 PM||||my dad drove for 30 years, let his licence run out and had to retake test. Dont do like he did and run a red lite. It wont be as tough as you think, just do what youve learned.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Hank is Here||02-11-2001||06:34 PM||||Well I failed once but oh well.  They got me on parellel parknig, I parked fine.  But the thing was this was in the middle of a parknig lot which was conned off, I didn't use my turn signals cause I thought I was in the middle of nowhere.  <BR>Here is one I learned to parellel park a tractor trailer during my one CDL test, nailed it perfect having having never done it before.  <BR>Today I know the fellow who passes me on all four of my different driving tests.  Every time I go to the DOT I stop by and talk with him for a while.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000014||fropuff||02-11-2001||07:18 PM||||Okay, I started a list on what I need to know.  You can add more if you want.  Thanks.<P>1) Don't speed.<BR>2) Stop before the white line.<BR>3) Stop before the sidewalk when leaving lot.<BR>4) Signal 100 feet prior.<BR>5) Watch for signs.<BR>6) Get into lane closest me.<BR>7) When turning left, don't enter crosswalk/intersection when I cannot go.<BR>8) Stop for three seconds when turning right on red.<BR>9) SMOG  (signal, mirrors, over the shoulder, go.)<BR>10) Don't turn wheels when I cannot turn right away; wait until I can go, then turn them.  Automatic failure.<BR>11) Signal when parking.<BR>12) Buckle up before touching the key.<BR>13) Watch for intersections; hover foot over brake on uncontrolled intersections.<P>That's all I've got so far.  Thanks for the replies.  I hope I get an "easy" instructor.  These ones aren't that hard on kids.  One girl in my class failed parking and still got it.  Thanks again.  13 hours and 45 minutes to go...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000015||loafer87gt||02-11-2001||08:04 PM||||I'm still mentally scarred from the my first drivers test. The rather overweight lady that was testing me flipped down the passenger side visor in my brother's Civic and proceeded to pop her pimples while looking in the visor mirror. It was so gross, AFTER passing the test, I phoned in and filed a compaint about the ladies behavior.||||reg||1
Z||000016||btoth||02-11-2001||10:17 PM||||that list you put together reminds me of what i had to do while taking my mail truck driving test for the post office.  that was not fun... right hand drive is very weird.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||7
Z||000017||Tigger||02-11-2001||11:00 PM||||Pick up a driving game like Midtown Madness and go like nuts.  Put the police patrol meter to the max.  If you even try to do something stupid they'll come after you, that's when the fun begins...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Good Luck!||||reg||1
Z||000018||fropuff||02-12-2001||04:16 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Enough said.  Pretty easy test.  Snowed 3-4" last night though.  I thought that I was screwed, but it actually turned to my favor.  Only thing I did wrong was take a turn a little wide.  Who cares.  Now I get to drive to school in style!  Thanks for the help.  It helped my nervousness a little.  Thanks. <P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
